#: ../../docstring
#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports.standard_funcs.pdf_extract.rst:28:<autosummary>:1
#: freeports.standard_funcs.pdf_extract.AssetsColumn:1 of
msgid "The Python shim of one numeric column of the assets pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.standard_funcs.pdf_extract.AssetsColumn:3 of
msgid ""
"A column is an anchor plus the search window hung off it, and the three "
"belong together: the window is measured in multiples of *that* anchor's "
"bounding box, so a vector without its anchor means nothing. Grouping them"
" is what lets the assets pipe take three column arguments instead of nine"
" loose ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.standard_funcs.pdf_extract.AssetsColumn:8 of
msgid ""
"The defaults are the native constructor's, and they are the shape of the "
"common case: the number sits on the label's own row, to its right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.standard_funcs.pdf_extract.AssetsColumn:11 of
msgid ""
"The Python selection is kept beside the native one so that the `anchor` "
"getter can hand back what was passed in: the native form is an either-or "
"type the shim cannot rebuild from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractAssetsStandard:3
msgid ""
"Each of the three numeric columns is one [`PyAssetsColumn`], which is "
"what the native type has always been: an anchor and the window hung off "
"it. The signature used to spell the three apart into nine flat keywords "
"and regroup them here, which meant a format could pass a vector to one "
"column and a multiplier to another without anything noticing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractDocClassifyStandard:1
msgid ""
"The document classifier: the page says the document is of `pattern` if "
"**every** selection finds something. `pattern` is a (possibly partial) "
"format name; one that does not read as a pattern is a `ValueError` "
"carrying the reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractFundStandard:3
msgid ""
"`join` makes the block **every** selected line joined by that separator, "
"in reading order, instead of the first one — `join=\" \"` for a title "
"split where a long dash falls, `join=\"\"` for one split inside a word. "
"Absent, the pipe takes the first line, which is what every format writing"
" the name on one line wants and what this pipe has always done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractFundStandard:8
msgid ""
"It is a keyword and not a second function because the two are the same "
"algorithm with a parameter: a formats repository had written the joining "
"variant as a Python shim of its own — nine lines of geometry plus the "
"reading order and the squeezing — and the only thing it changed was this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractInvestmentsStandard:3
msgid ""
"**A divergence absorbed here:** two of the selections are accepted and "
"ignored. That is not an oversight — they were never used on this side "
"either, the currency and the management company arriving from sibling "
"pipes. The native type, having no compatibility constraint, does not have"
" them at all, but author modules still pass them, so the Python signature"
" must still accept them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractLabelledValueStandard:4
msgid ""
"Three positional arguments, and every keyword optional: the defaults are "
"the label's own line, the first match and no further constraint, which is"
" the shape twenty-one formats of the reference collection write the "
"management company in. See "
"[`crate::formats_utils::pdf_extract::labelled_value`] for what each "
"placement means and for what `reach` and `across` are measured in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractLabelledValueStandard:10
msgid ""
"`reach` and `across` are separate keywords rather than one `window` tuple"
" so that a format can set the one it needs and leave the other at the "
"default its placement carries — the two have different defaults for "
"`BELOW` and for `RIGHT`, and a tuple would force both to be written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractSectionStandard:4
msgid ""
"`family` omesso significa *la prossima riga con la stessa coppia (font, "
"corpo) dell'intestazione*, che è il difetto misurato; passarne una "
"selezione lo sostituisce, ed è il caso di AMUNDI-EN24 p510, dove "
"intestazioni e righe hanno la stessa tipografia. `bottom` accetta una "
"selezione o un'ordinata. `rows`, se dato, chiede le coordinate di tabella"
" nei metadati: `True` scopre le colonne, una `TableConfig` le dichiara."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractSfdrSignStandard:5
msgid ""
"Two positional arguments and every keyword optional: the question's "
"anchor and the pair of answer labels, affirmative first. See "
"[`crate::formats_utils::pdf_extract::sfdr_sign`] for what each recognizer"
" looks for, and why the tick characters have to be named rather than "
"guessed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.PdfExtractSfdrSignStandard:10
msgid ""
"`ticked`, `blank` and `marks_by_font` **add to** the measured table "
"rather than replacing it, so a format that meets a new typography "
"declares only what is new."
msgstr ""

